.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt BMI270 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bmi270g
.Nd Bosch BMI270 accelerometer and gyroscope
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "bmi270g* at iic?"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver attaches to a device-tree node compatible with
.Qq bosch,bmi270
and reports accelerometer and gyroscope axes through
.Xr sysmon_envsys 9 .
The Bosch base configuration is loaded at attach, and both sensors are enabled
at 100 Hz with a 2 g accelerometer range and a 2000 degree/s gyroscope range.
Accelerometer values are integer micrometres per second squared (um/s^2);
gyroscope values are integer millidegrees per second (mdps).
.Pp
Initialization uses the public Bosch BMI270 SensorAPI base configuration from
the common Ports source package. It validates chip identity and propagates I2C
and configuration errors. Espressif custom Circle/Toy firmware is not used.
The source is Bosch BMI270 SensorAPI 2.113.0 at commit
41129fcfe39c583ee5462d79195741945d51c1fe, under its BSD-3-Clause license.
.Sh DEVICE TREE
.Bl -tag -width "compatible"
.It compatible
.Qq bosch,bmi270
.It reg
I2C address, 0x69 on the ESP-Mosaico V1.2 board.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr envstat 8 ,
.Xr sysmon_envsys 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in EmberBSD 11.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Bosch Sensortec
for the SensorAPI.
.An The EmberBSD Project
for the driver integration.
